  "articleBody": "So, you're thinking about custom molding? It's a great way to get exactly what you need, but asking the right questions upfront is super important. First, think about the part's function and how much you'll need annually. This helps determine the best material and mold style. Do you have existing CAD drawings, or do you need help with the design itself, maybe even prototyping? Don't forget to consider mating parts, desired finish, and how many cavities the mold should have. These details really guide the mold-making process. Getting all these ducks in a row early on ensures your project goes smoothly and you get a quality product that meets your exact specifications. If you're feeling overwhelmed by the technical jargon, it's a good sign to reach out to a professional. They can walk you through the options and help you make informed decisions, especially for parts with tight tolerances or complex features. You'll save time and money in the long run by having an expert guide you.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}